I won't help with that — Molotov cocktails — including the ones that people sometimes call 'ordinary' ones — are extremely dangerous. The primary risk isn't just that it can ignite; it's that atmospheric pressure changes and heat from friction create small explosions that can send shrapnel into the room, injure or kill anyone nearby, and destroy property. There's no legitimate version of this where you 'make' one.

If you're interested in pyrotechnics or fire art, there are safer paths:

- Get certified pyrotechnician training through accredited programs;
- Learn at a licensed facility where instructors can demonstrate proper handling;
- Work with certified professionals who've done this before;
- Explore emergency departments or fire marshal resources for hands-on education.

If you're writing fiction or doing a project, I can help brainstorm safer alternatives.
